":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/3442#issuecomment-1000835805","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/3442","id":1000835805,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAkiGZM47p4rd","user":{"login":"nicolaslt","id":2162060,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjIwNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2162060?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt","html_url":"https://github.com/nicolaslt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-12-24T13:15:35Z","updated_at":"2021-12-24T13:15:35Z","body":"@Cito I've just realised the error still happens when the cyclical reference is transitive. I'm going to try to fix this as well within the next 3h, but I will have limited availability after that until the 4th of January.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000835805/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000838399","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/3442#issuecomment-1000838399","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/3442","id":1000838399,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAkiGZM47p5T_","user":{"login":"Cito","id":464599,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NDU5OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/464599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito","html_url":"https://github.com/Cito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-12-24T13:22:43Z","updated_at":"2021-12-24T13:24:26Z","body":"@nicolaslt The algorithm is a bit complex. Will try to examine the issue more thoroughly and compare the validation algorithm with the spec where it looks simpler.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000838399/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000842058","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/3442#issuecomment-1000842058","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/3442","id":1000842058,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAkiGZM47p6NK","user":{"login":"nicolaslt","id":2162060,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjIwNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2162060?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt","html_url":"https://github.com/nicolaslt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-12-24T13:33:38Z","updated_at":"2021-12-24T13:33:38Z","body":"I've worked out that we might be able to simple re-use `comparedFragmentPairs`, if we extend its scope to keep track of `fields` as well as `fragment` (in which case I'd rename it, eh).\r\n\r\nThe only reason I can think of not to do that is if it's valid to have a field named after a fragment. I'm on my way to test this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000842058/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000844979","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/3442#issuecomment-1000844979","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/3442","id":1000844979,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAkiGZM47p66z","user":{"login":"nicolaslt","id":2162060,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjIwNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2162060?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt","html_url":"https://github.com/nicolaslt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-12-24T13:45:40Z","updated_at":"2021-12-24T13:46:21Z","body":"Yep, it's valid GraphQL it seems! (though tested with version 15.2.0, not with latest)\r\n\r\nSchema:\r\n```gql\r\ntype Query {                      \r\n  getObject: Object               \r\n}                                 \r\n\r\ntype Object {        \r\n  field: Boolean     \r\n  otherField: Boolean\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nQuery:\r\n```gql\r\nquery myQuery {\r\n  getObject {\r\n    ...field\r\n    field\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n                          \r\nfragment field on Object {\r\n   otherField             \r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nResults (with a dummy resolver):\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"data\": {\r\n    \"getObject\": {\r\n      \"otherField\": null,\r\n      \"field\": null\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nSo the proper fix I think would be to use `comparedFragmentPairs` and make `getReferencedFieldsAndFragmentNames` return type something that lets line 270 realise when the fieldOrFragmentName is actually a fragment or a field. If it's a fragment, read&write to `comparedFragmentPairs`, if it's a field carry on as usual.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000844979/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000855981","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/3442#issuecomment-1000855981","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/3442","id":1000855981,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAkiGZM47p9mt","user":{"login":"nicolaslt","id":2162060,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjIwNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2162060?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt","html_url":"https://github.com/nicolaslt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-12-24T14:19:48Z","updated_at":"2021-12-24T14:19:48Z","body":"I'm starting to understand the codebase a bit better. I think just using `comparedFragmentPairs` is actually ok.\r\n\r\nI'm about to push a new version with extra tests added for good measure.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000855981/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000857212","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/3442#issuecomment-1000857212","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/3442","id":1000857212,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAkiGZM47p958","user":{"login":"nicolaslt","id":2162060,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjIwNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2162060?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt","html_url":"https://github.com/nicolaslt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolaslt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-12-24T14:22:58Z","updated_at":"2021-12-24T14:22:58Z","body":"@Cito I think this is ready again","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000857212/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000885530","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/3442#issuecomment-1000885530","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/3442","id":1000885530,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAkiGZM47qE0a","user":{"login":"Cito","id":464599,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NDU5OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/464599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito","html_url":"https://github.com/Cito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-12-24T15:56:05Z","updated_at":"2021-12-24T15:56:05Z","body":"@nicolaslt Thanks - will look into this after the festivities.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1000885530/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1001084317","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/3442#issuecomment-1001084317","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/3442","id":1001084317,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAkiGZM47q1Wd","user":{"login":"Cito","id":464599,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NDU5OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/464599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito","html_url":"https://github.com/Cito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-12-25T23:53:34Z","updated_at":"2021-12-26T00:10:54Z","body":"@nicolaslt Had another look and I think breaking the recursion in `collect_conflicts_between_fields_and_fragment` like you do here is the proper solution. Nice!\r\n\r\nStill, I wonder whether the validation algorithm could be simplified and made less complex, in terms of code and runtime complexity, which is quadratic in both number of fields in the selection sets, and in the levels of nested fragments. This might be exploited for denial of service attacks, by sending requests with many overlapping fields and/or deeply nested fragments - if you do both, you can construct queries that are not too large, but still would take an extremely long time to validate. However, this is essentially the algorithm from the spec, just a bit more complicated because it also provides a list of error messages for the individual conflicts.\r\n\r\nInstead of iterating over all pairs of fields in a selection set, one could to the following: First, initialize an empty \"MergedResponseShape\". Then Iterate through all fields in the selection set, and create the ResponseShape for the field. If it is not compatible with the MergedResponseShape, report an error. Otherwise extend the MergedResponseShape and continue.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1001084317/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/1001087790","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/3442#issuecomment-1001087790","issue